cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Prompt Injection Eval"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cavaletto
    given-names: Federico
repository-code: "https://github.com/fcavaletto/prompt-injection-eval"
url: "https://fcavaletto.github.io/prompt-injection-eval/"
version: 0.5.0
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-12
abstract: >-
  A small local evaluation harness for indirect prompt injection in open-weight
  language models. Version 0.4.0 adds an adaptive-attack study: strategies
  written after reading the prompt defenses, tuned on one set of documents and
  scored once on a held-out set, against a generic document-trust rule and a
  datamarking defense. Version 0.5.0 adds the document delivered as a tool
  result, with a placement control, and a quiet-attack measure. Scoring is by
  deterministic rules. It is a diagnostic, not a production safety guarantee.
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - language models
  - evaluation
  - ai safety
